### Reading These Numbers

- **Observed unique work identities**: deduplicated union of Jira issues, task records, and authenticated bot PR/MR records. Every identity in this union is counted as Rehor work.
- **Observed Jira-key identities**: work identities that can be tied to a Jira key, including keys outside baseline filter.
- **Observed non-Jira identities**: valid Rehor task or PR/MR records without detected Jira key references. These include GitHub/GitLab, manual, grooming, and other workflows.
- **Complete historical total**: permanently unrecoverable from current systems. Local pre-deployment activity has no reliable central record. Treat it as a fixed historical caveat; its share of total Rehor work will become progressively smaller as post-deployment observed work accumulates.

