## Completion And Acceptance

Jira completion and Git merge acceptance are separate outcomes. A Jira issue can be completed without a PR/MR, and a PR/MR can be merged while Jira state is delayed or absent.

| Outcome | Completed / accepted | Denominator | Rate |
|---|---:|---:|---:|
| Jira issues completed | {{ jira_completed }} | {{ jira_count }} Jira issues | {{ ((jira_completed / jira_count * 100)|round(1)) if jira_count else 'unknown' }}% |
| GitHub PRs merged | {{ gh_merged }} | {{ gh_merged + gh_closed_unmerged }} decided PRs | {{ ((gh_merged / (gh_merged + gh_closed_unmerged) * 100)|round(1)) if (gh_merged + gh_closed_unmerged) else 'unknown' }}% |
| GitLab MRs merged | {{ gl_merged }} | {{ gl_merged + gl_closed_unmerged }} decided MRs | {{ ((gl_merged / (gl_merged + gl_closed_unmerged) * 100)|round(1)) if (gl_merged + gl_closed_unmerged) else 'unknown' }}% |
| Combined PRs/MRs accepted | {{ gh_merged + gl_merged }} | {{ merge_decisions }} decided PRs/MRs | {{ merge_acceptance_pct if merge_acceptance_pct is not none else 'unknown' }}% |

Acceptance denominator excludes open PRs/MRs. This measures merge acceptance among decided submissions, not all attempted work. It does not measure code quality, reviewer effort, or value delivered.

